  <SiteShell>
    <h2>Welcome to my website</h2>
    <p>You may be thinking to yourself, "Oliver, your website looks a little crazy." I know right. It's an homage to the early internet and GeoCities era of personal site dev and it has been a ton of fun to work on.</p>
    <p>If you don't know me, you can probably guess my name :^) I'm a CS student at UW-Madison though I was born and raised in Seattle. At Madison I helped run the Undergraduate Projects Lab, a student lab that's been around since the 1980s. I helped plan various events and Wisconsin's largest hackathon. I spent the last two summers at Amazon writing internal tools for the AGI org. I graduate in December 2026.</p>
    <p>Most of my free time goes into hanging with friends and building things. Some recent ones: a  Tauri desktop app for mapping out social graphs in Neo4j, and a Go bot that watches company career pages so I don't have to. This site renovation (renovation #4 actually) is the latest project. It's not done. It may never be done. That's kind of the point.</p>
    <p>Off the computer it's reading, fishing, and listening to music (Recently <a class="lastfm-artist" href="https://www.last.fm/user/oliverohrt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Earl Sweatshirt</a>). Right now I'm studying abroad in Thailand, so expect blog posts about that when the blog exists.</p>
    <p>Thanks for stopping by. Sign the guestbook on your way out (there is no guestbook yet).</p>
  </SiteShell>
